From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arpit Kumar Jaiswal <arpit1.mitmpl2024@learner.manipal.edu>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:36:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-uvm: return the status of EGM DMA mappings

uvm_gpu_map_cpu_pages_for_egm() recorded DMA link, sync and missing DMA IOVA API
failures in status and then returned NV_OK, so callers used a mapping that didn't exist.

From upstream PR 1423 (Arpit Kumar Jaiswal), without its host test script.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c
index 6d42f184..3677ff4a 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c
@@ -4115,7 +4115,7 @@ done:
     }
 
     *dma_address_out = dma_addr;
-    return NV_OK;
+    return status;
 }
 
 NV_STATUS uvm_gpu_map_cpu_pages(uvm_gpu_t *gpu, struct page *page, size_t size, NvU64 *dma_address_out)
